{# =====================================================================
   Visitor globe — "where our guests are right now".

   Drop-in on each homepage, BETWEEN the testimonials and the booking
   form:  {% include "partials/visitor-globe.njk" %}

   Placement is deliberate. The card is social proof — a live count of
   people planning a Bali trip, and the countries they are reading from —
   so it belongs immediately after the reviews and immediately before the
   booking CTA, at the point where a visitor is deciding. It is also low
   enough down the page that the widget's own lazy-loading (a ~105 KB
   country topology and a requestAnimationFrame loop) never touches the
   critical path; only the visit POST is eager, so the total keeps meaning
   "visitors" and not "people who scrolled this far".

   All text inside the component is localized by /js/visitor-globe.js from
   <html lang>, the same way /js/reviews.js localizes the testimonials —
   shadow DOM is unreachable from this file or from css/styles.css.

   The --vg-* custom properties below are the ENTIRE theming surface for
   the component. The five canvas colours are parsed as HEX ONLY; rgb(),
   hsl() and color-mix() silently fall back to the built-in defaults, so
   do not switch them to var() references or colour functions.
   ===================================================================== #}
<section class="globe-section" id="visitors">
  <h2 class="section-title reveal">{{ ui.globe_title[lang] or ui.globe_title.en }}</h2>
  <div class="globe-wrap">
    <visitor-globe></visitor-globe>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .globe-section {
    padding: 60px 50px 80px;
    background-color: var(--ocean-deep);
  }
  /* The section sits between two light bands (white reviews above, sand
     booking form below); the dark ground is what keeps all three from
     running together, and it makes the globe read as lit rather than flat. */
  .globe-section .section-title {
    color: #fff;
    margin-top: 0;
  }
  .globe-wrap {
    max-width: 1020px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .globe-wrap visitor-globe {
    --vg-ink: #1f2a30;
    --vg-muted: #5f6f78;
    --vg-surface: #ffffff;
    --vg-border: #e6ddcf;
    --vg-radius: var(--radius);
    --vg-shadow: 0 18px 50px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.28);
    --vg-accent: #00557f;

    /* Canvas — literal hex only (see the note above). */
    --vg-land: #0e5b73;    /* continents  */
    --vg-ocean: #dbeef6;   /* water       */
    --vg-rim: #00557f;     /* outline     */
    --vg-past: #ff6b4a;    /* places seen — brand coral */
    --vg-current: #13b5a6; /* newest place — brand aqua */
    --vg-live: #15803d;    /* the online-now dot */
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .globe-section {
      padding: 40px 20px 60px;
    }
  }
</style>

<script src="/js/visitor-globe.js" defer></script>
